Assuming the driver does not invent the error itself which I think is
unlikely this is the drive telling you it has big problems. Media
errors can sometimes be cured by sending the drive a SCSI FORMAT UNIT cmd
and waiting for it to reassign the bad blocks. Note that it has a finite
number of spare blocks.

If you have loads of errors reported it could also have developed a bad 
head or a bad head amplifier chip or something nasty like that. 

If this is the case it is either in for a warranty claim 
(if it is not too old) or a trip to the dumpster.

Hope this helps,

Wilko
